      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For resisting daily scuff marks and micro-abrasions, LVT is generally the most resilient due to its flexible composition, which absorbs minor impacts. Polished concrete is very tough against general wear but harder marks, especially heavier scuffs, can become permanently etched or visible in the finish. Natural stone, while beautiful, is the most vulnerable to surface abrasions and scratches that can dull its polished finish over time.",
